    "_about": "THE MOOSE (Alces alces; 2026-11-08, generator tools/creaturegen/ungulates/gen.py, on the deer frame): a bull of about 2 m at the shoulder -- very long slender legs, pale grey-brown below the knee, under a short deep trunk; the high HUMP over the shoulders, the back falling to a lower rump; a short thick neck with a dark crest; the long heavy head hung forward and down, a Roman-nosed bridge ending in the great overhanging MUZZLE (a broad pendulous upper lip past the short lower jaw, slit nostrils on its front); large ears (the deer's `fin` ear mapped larger); the BELL, a hairy `fin` flap hanging from the throat; a short stump of a tail; dark brown, near black on the hump. The ANTLERS (bull only, `when: bull`), exactly mirrored: from each pedicle a short beam (a `horn`, flattened in the antler's plane) out and a little up, and on it two PALMS -- dished `fin` sheets rooted along the beam, each in its own plane: the brow palm reaching forward nearly level with four tines, the broad main palm rising back and up (its plane tipped 38 degrees back) with six, a cleft between them -- every tine a short `horn` on the palm's rim, turning a little up, its tip pale. Legs: the chamois' (ulib.legs_from), stretched. Variants `cow` (no antlers; shares the bull's shape build) and `calf`."
  },
